M9: I found a network of 18 resistors that matches all 27 measurements, and the answer was accepted. The largest gap between a computed and a measured resistance is 0.000492 ohms, just inside the 0.0005 ohm tolerance.  **How I found it:** 1. I started with a resistor on every one of the 66 possible node pairs and fitted the values to the measurements. 2. I removed the weakest resistor and refitted, repeating until 18 were left. 3. I then tried swapping single resistors to other node pairs, keeping any swap that reduced the error.  Most attempts got stuck with errors of about 0.15 to 1 ohm. One run reached about 0.0004 ohms, with every fitted value within 0.03 ohms of a value on the allowed list. I rounded each to that value and checked the result directly; that check gave the 0.000492 ohm figure.  **Submitted network (ohms):**  | Resistor | Between | Value | |---|---|---| | R1 | A – N1 | 28 | | R2 | A – N10 | 35 | | R3 | N4 – N5 | 147 | | R4 | A – N8 | 12 | | R5 | B – N3 | 180 | | R6 | B – N6 | 28 | | R7 | B – N9 | 21 | | R8 | N1 – N4 | 31 | | R9 | N1 – N5 | 147 | | R10 | N10 – N7 | 47 | | R11 | N10 – N9 | 31 | | R12 | N2 – N6 | 119 | | R13 | N2 – N7 | 11 | | R14 | N2 – N9 | 35 | | R15 | N3 – N4 | 119 | | R16 | N3 – N8 | 15 | | R17 | N5 – N8 | 35 | | R18 | N6 – N7 | 31 |  The scripts are in `/tmp/corral-claude-wa_08c0y`; `v.py` checks the final network and prints the submitted JSON.

